<!--
  Larova · Chinese (Simplified) strings.

  The directory is `values-zh`, not `values-b+zh+Hans`. Compose Multiplatform resources match on
  language and region, not on script, and Simplified is the only Chinese in the launch set
  (`zh-Hans` in locales_config.xml), so the bare language qualifier is what a phone set to
  zh-Hans-CN actually resolves to. A Traditional set later needs `values-zh-rTW` or `-rHK`.

  A translation, not a source: never fix wording here. Fix the English in values/strings.xml and
  re-translate. See docs/localization.md.

  **A model draft, not yet read by a native speaker.** docs/localization.md §5 names the three
  parts that must not ship on a machine draft — the help bar and contact sheet, the two view names,
  and the six templates.

  Chinese has one plural form, so every <plurals> below carries `other` alone.
-->
